          "distinct": true,
          "id": "154659c727e90c3f2ac415641b67c4419bff79c2",
          "message": "Stabilize chart dataset identity via datasetIdKey\n\nreact-chartjs-2 matches datasets across renders by their `label` by\ndefault. PropertiesBarChart sets `label: recipe.name || recipe.id`, so\nevery keystroke in the RecipeEditor name input shifts the label and\nmakes Chart.js treat the dataset as new — re-animating bars from zero.\nFpdGraph had a related workaround that baked `recipe.name` into line\nlabels for uniqueness.\n\nAdd a stable `id` derived from `recipe.id` (slot id \"Recipe\" / \"Ref A\",\nunchanged across edits) and pass `datasetIdKey=\"id\"` so dataset identity\nis decoupled from label content.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
