          "id": "547f5f3c5fe208a850a37ce1bf6e91d47de9faff",
          "message": "Improve balancing tests with quality reporting\n\nAdd best-effort and magnitude-disparate balancing cases plus insta\nsnapshot reports tracking per-target relative error across both\nsolvers, mirroring the compare_specs pattern.\n\n- Merge verify_balance_composition and assert_balance_within_ceiling\n  into one assert_balance_compositions with optional Epsilons and a\n  per-key KeyCeiling tolerance\n- Generalize CompCeiling to KeyCeiling, a shared per-key threshold\n  table reused by the specs and balancing tests\n- Cover real-world disparate scenarios (fat-vs-calorie, coupled\n  cocoa, high-MSNF, sorbet POD/PAC, boozy ABV/PAC) built from named\n  DATABASE ingredients via comps_from_names\n- Add is_ratio_key / get_balanceable_comp_keys to exclude ratio keys,\n  which break the linear balancing model\n- Remove IMPORTANT_TARGET_KEYS in favor of get_balanceable_comp_keys,\n  now the target-key source for both tests and benchmarks\n- Extract root_mean_square into tests::util with unit tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
