          "distinct": true,
          "id": "896ae440e003b8a6f0ee207ead0b815b6924db1d",
          "message": "Add balancing target validation and entry point\n\nAdd `balance_compositions`, a validated entry point that runs\n`validate_balancing_targets` and rejects error-severity issues\n(ratio-key, non-finite, or duplicate targets) via the new\n`Error::InvalidBalancingTargets` before solving. Warning-severity\nissues (unaffectable, unreachable-range, and palette-derived dominance\ninfeasibility) are reported but do not gate the solve.\n\nDiagnostics are modeled as `BalancingReport` / `BalancingIssue` /\n`Severity` (serde-serializable), with `Display` impls in display.rs.\n`choose_solver` centralizes solver choice (nnls in production); the raw\n`_nnls` / `_nalgebra` solvers remain unguarded. `Recipe::balance` now\nroutes through the entry point. Also adds the `is_subset` /\n`is_within_range` epsilon helpers in validate.rs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
