          "distinct": true,
          "id": "73402e682e78b39184f1b8446ef455b63f43bb53",
          "message": "Add per-key priority to balancing\n\nTargets can be marked High or Critical priority, weighting their rows\nmore heavily in the least-squares solve so they are fit more closely\nat the expense of the rest. Normal (the default) maps to a weight-1\nmultiplier, leaving existing behavior unchanged.\n\n- Priority enum: Normal/High/Critical -> 1/5/25 weight multiplier\n- The two solvers take numeric per-key weights; balance_compositions\n  and Recipe::balance take the abstract Priority and translate it\n- row_weights folds the multiplier into each target row, never the\n  mass-balance sum row, so priority cannot weaken mass balance\n\nValidate the priority list via the existing BalancingReport: a\nduplicate priority key is an error, and a priority for a key with no\ntarget is a warning.\n\nAlso add \"unprioritized\" to the cspell dictionary for the new docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-03T11:05:01-04:00",
          "tree_id": "91a767b647561ee70bf3e14c557b24ddba21ae87",
