          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6f6cbe25f1393fe4c275469fb730d08635df2d0f",
          "message": "Extract ratio keys into RatioKey, a PropKey arm\n\nRatio properties (AbsPAC, EmulsifiersPerFat, StabilizersPerWater) were\nCompKey variants, conflating non-additive ratios with extensive\nquantities and forcing scattered special-casing across balancing and\nthe app.\n\nMove them into a dedicated RatioKey enum that forms a third arm of\nPropKey (alongside CompKey and FpdKey). CompKey is now all-extensive,\nso isCompKeyQuantity is deleted and isPropKeyQuantity collapses to\nisCompKey. RatioKey::parts/scope replace the free ratio_key_* fns, and\na KeyScope (Mix/Ingredient/Both) soft hint filters mix-context\ndropdowns via isPropKeyMixScope.\n\nBalancing targets move from (CompKey, f64) to a BalanceKey union\n(Comp | Ratio), keeping a clean typed solver. The WASM edge resolves\nflat key names to BalanceKey, so the JS balancing wire format is\nunchanged; Composition.get_ratio and ratio display/scope helpers are\nexposed for the TS package and app.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
