          "id": "627bd407fd803de78ea1cc686191e19a3b41b530",
          "message": "Stabilize chart visual snapshots\n\nChart.js draws to a <canvas>, so Playwright's CSS-only animation\nfreezing can't stop its default ~1s entry animation. Emulate reduced\nmotion in the visual project and disable the animation under it, so\npopulated charts settle to a stable final frame.\n\nEmpty charts still show run-to-run aliasing differences in their\ncanvas text, unrelated to animation. Fill the calculator layout tests\nwith a recipe so their charts render populated (and stable), and give\nthe two inherently-empty chart panel snapshots a small maxDiffPixels\nbudget that absorbs the text shimmer without hiding a real regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
