          "distinct": true,
          "id": "cefb77b1063cc12723408360af6abb13be83f817",
          "message": "Track per-source protein subtypes in composition\n\nMake SolidsBreakdown generic over a new ProteinComponents trait so\neach solid source carries its own protein type: MilkProteins\n(casein/whey), EggProteins (white/yolk), and SimpleProteins (total)\nfor cocoa/nut/other and aggregates. Invalid combinations (e.g. casein\non egg) are now compile errors.\n\nAdd Casein, Whey, WhiteProteins, and YolkProteins CompKeys, nested\nunder the milk/egg protein rollups in the display hierarchy.\n\nDairy specs split protein into casein/whey via the MSNF split\nconstants; EggSpec provisionally records all protein as yolk until\nwhite/yolk support lands.\n\nDairy test fixtures now hold explicit casein/whey literals rather\nthan calling the production split helper, so the split ratio is\nverified independently rather than circularly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-21T22:16:01-04:00",
          "tree_id": "5c033f13c7cbd6c892e1f7a6b1ae0121a3f3407b",
          "url": "https://github.com/ramonrsv/sci-cream/commit/cefb77b1063cc12723408360af6abb13be83f817"
