          "distinct": true,
          "id": "65b72fd083e7188b44555d8b32d19200310eba78",
          "message": "Collapse theme color tokens onto the CSS cascade\n\nSwitch semantic colors from `@theme inline` (which bakes literal values\ninto utilities) to plain `@theme`, so utilities reference `var()`. Each\n`-light`/`-dark` pair collapses to one canonical token with a light\ndefault and a single `.dark` override; short aliases follow lazily.\n\nThis drops the ~30 pure-token `@variant dark` blocks in globals.css and\nthe `X-lt dark:X-dk` utility twins in JSX. Blocks switching literal\nTailwind palette colors (select-option, signin-*, btn-primary, etc.)\nkeep a slimmed `@variant dark`.\n\nOn the JS side ThemeColor tokens are now single cascading vars, so\ngetJsColor (which suffixed -light/-dark) is gone; getColor / getCssColor\ntake a Color | ThemeColor union. The charts read colors via getColor and\nkeep a bare useTheme() subscription to repaint the canvas on theme flip.\n\nResolved colors are unchanged, so the visual suite passes without\nregeneration (175 visual + 891 unit tests green).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-24T22:52:48-04:00",
          "tree_id": "fa54058f0525a5cf3266eddc0701177cd4078b2c",
