          "distinct": true,
          "id": "814aa95eb75d09190b651932d1945075b56f968c",
          "message": "Add continuous auto-balance toggle to Watchers\n\nAdd an \"Auto\" toggle to the Watchers toolbar that continuously\nre-balances the main recipe whenever a target, priority, or the batch\ntotal changes. The mode is session-only and off by default.\n\nEditing the recipe in the RecipeEditor cancels the mode via a new\nonUserEdit callback, distinguishing user edits from the balancer's own\nwrites (both flow through the same recipe context). The toggle state is\nowned by the calculator page so the sibling editor can reset it.\n\nThe auto-balance effect runs in useLayoutEffect so the re-balanced\nrecipe is flushed before paint, avoiding a one-frame stale-delta\nflicker. It is keyed only on user-controlled inputs, so the balancer's\nwrite to the recipe cannot re-trigger it. When a validation error stops\nauto-balancing, the toggle grays out and its tooltip explains why.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-03T22:07:52-04:00",
          "tree_id": "745f3f9f4152fd3f4e0d022001208f8dc57e87a9",
