          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d921c2e3b250c89f2ecd25a7cd11a9c5293be908",
          "message": "Add normalization-mode toggle to properties chart\n\nAdd a toolbar toggle to pick how each property normalizes onto its\n0-100 track: Full Spread (union of range/value/refs/target, the\ndefault), Target/Value centered (the anchor sits at 50%), and Fill\nRange (the acceptable range frames the padded track). The strategies\nresolve through `resolveMeterDomain` in range-meter, all feeding the\nshared `valueToMeterPct` mapping. Selection persists per panel.\n\nFloor a data-driven spread to `MIN_SPREAD_FRAC` of the values'\nmagnitude, so a value matching its target stays centered instead of\nbeing flung to opposite ends of the track by floating-point noise.\n\nFix empty/zero properties drawing red zero-bars: the chart now\nmirrors WatcherCard, treating an absent or zero value as no bar (only\nthe acceptable-range band remains) rather than coercing it to 0.\n\nCover the new math, the NormMode select, and the chart wiring with\nunit tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-06T23:49:12-04:00",
