          "distinct": true,
          "id": "13aa470b1382f682513ef5aa981af943946feaa1",
          "message": "Add container colors to make-recipe batches\n\nA recipe can now wear a color matching the physical tub it is mixed\nin, picked from the recipe's own badge in the builder and carried in\nthe share link. Colors are data, not styling.\n\nThe palette gains White and Black beside the eight CVD-validated\nhues. Being achromatic, they are painted as solid fills rather than\ntints: a tint washes away the lightness they are identified by,\nwhich erases one chip per theme. Each solid names the ink its fill\nneeds, since it cannot inherit the page's text color. All ten are\nre-stepped per theme, as the hues already were, so black no longer\ncoincides with the dark page background.\n\nThe color rides the wire as a name rather than a slot index, in a\nnew optional field. No payload version bump: comparePayloadVersion\nhas no \"older\" branch, so raising the version would reject every\nlink already shared, whereas an optional field is compatible in\nboth directions. A name this app does not know is dropped rather\nthan failing the link, since only amounts are worth that.\n\nColor is excluded from the checkoff hash, so recoloring a batch\nnever discards weighing progress.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-20T18:18:53-04:00",
          "tree_id": "66364510aff95d8d35077bd0324b5bba100c62be",
