          "distinct": true,
          "id": "381476e892c15b79e008144d02d4e4ba4abedd8e",
          "message": "Use verify/verifyDefined for precondition checks\n\nverify() now takes `unknown` + an `asserts condition` signature, so\nTS narrows after the call instead of leaving `!` non-null hacks behind.\nA new verifyDefined<T> narrows to NonNullable<T> for the common\nsingle-value nullish-check shape.\n\nMigrate sites that were silently returning on a \"this shouldn't happen\"\nstate to throw instead, so a future bug surfaces as a thrown error\nrather than a no-op:\n\n- recipes/page.tsx: 3 handler guards (delete recipe / version /\n  update version comments)\n- _elements/tables/recipe.tsx: 2 manual throw blocks in save flows\n  rewritten as inverted verify() calls\n- lib/database/seed.ts: 2 `if (!user) throw` calls converted to\n  verifyDefined(user, ...)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-19T12:34:29-04:00",
          "tree_id": "7a6a6fec535fba750c25bca0c32e9bb1ea231e6c",
