          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ca77c923f4b0f2245162735043bfcf732d828f37",
          "message": "Align search columns with a toolbar-height spacer\n\nThe ingredient- and recipe-search detail panels offset their left column\nwith a hardcoded mt-8.25 (33px) so the JSON/recipe table lines up with\nthe adjacent view's data table, which sits below a selects toolbar. That\noffset broke when the toolbar's height changed. Replace it with a\nToolbarSpacer — an invisible single-row Select that occupies the real\ntoolbar height — so the columns align without a magic number.\n\nSingle-row only: if the adjacent toolbar wraps, the spacer under-reserves\nby a row. Acceptable for now since the single-select composition toolbar\nnever wraps and the offset is minor where it can.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-11T14:59:41-04:00",
          "tree_id": "ae0316b6fb9d8ac78e753eb3d96c92145efad245",
