          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ce92dcbff7d46ffecd1d843528c28617d6ea2833",
          "message": "Add Low balancing priority level\n\nIntroduces Priority::Low (weight 0.2) below Priority::Normal,\nmirroring the existing High and Critical levels above it.\n\n- Rust: adds Low variant to Priority enum; weight constants are now\n  derived from PRIORITY_LEVEL_FACTOR = 5 for the full ladder\n  (Low 0.2 · Normal 1 · High 5 · Critical 25); adds Low < Normal\n  assertion to the weight-ordering test\n- TS: adds Priority.Low = \"Low\" to the balancing.ts enum\n- App: extends PRIORITY_CYCLE to [Low, Normal, High, Critical] and\n  adds the blue ChevronDown PriorityMarker for Low; updates\n  PrioritiesMap JSDoc to reflect that sub-Normal entries are now stored\n- Tests: adds visual regression snapshots for all four priority states;\n  fixes two unit tests whose assertions assumed Critical wraps to Normal\n  (now wraps to Low) and that the map-sparseness test used Critical as\n  the starting point (now uses Low, which correctly advances to Normal)\n\n* Decrease `MIN_PRIORITY_EFFECT_PP` from 10.0 -> 6.0 for new tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-14T01:47:49-04:00",
          "tree_id": "18de1ee504750c11a6366c6a60c8a7e0683c54d4",
