          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f2377f895508a75c0d877d0f7dbd7c3a5992949a",
          "message": "Tolerate rounded targets in feasibility warnings\n\nThe balancer's target-feasibility warnings compared targets against\npalette bands using COMPOSITION_EPSILON (1e-13), but the app rounds\ntargets to display precision (~0.01-0.1). A rounded target thus fell\njust outside narrow or pinned bands, raising spurious warnings no input\ncould satisfy (e.g. a single-source MSNF:MilkFat ratio pinned to one\nvalue).\n\nAdd an optional relative tolerance to validate_balancing_targets: None\nkeeps the exact-precision behaviour, so the library and other consumers\nare unchanged; the app passes a small value matched to its display\nprecision. The tolerance flows into the reachability, palette-ratio, and\nstructural warning checks via new is_subset_rel / is_within_range_rel /\nare_equal_rel helpers (the strict variants now delegate with rel_tol =\n0). Warnings are advisory and never gate a solve, so this only\nsuppresses non-actionable noise.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-02T17:44:44-04:00",
          "tree_id": "07e00c5b625d559ec04570c77c98d1a6bb103d94",
          "url": "https://github.com/ramonrsv/sci-cream/commit/f2377f895508a75c0d877d0f7dbd7c3a5992949a"
