          "distinct": true,
          "id": "4e4a14e82d924e167edcca2d84c23fc4ca3ad1af",
          "message": "Add optional batch-total input to Watchers toolbar\n\nExpose a \"Total (g)\" input in the Watchers toolbar that behaves like a\ntarget input: when it holds a value, Balance sizes the recipe to that\ntotal (via balance_recipe's total_amount); when empty it is inert and\nBalance infers the total from the live recipe sum. The value persists in\nlocalStorage under a new watcher-total key.\n\nThe input renders only when balancing is fully wired (both wasmBridge and\nonApplyBalancedMain), since the total is only meaningful with the Balance\npath present.\n\nPer-row rounding when writing balanced grams back can leave the summed\ntotal slightly off the balancer's target; documented as acceptable.\n\n* There is a small regression where in the `mobile-small-portrait`\n  layout all the balancing component don't fit in one row of the toolbar\n  and so overflow cutting off part of the 'Balance' button; needs a fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-03T18:29:03-04:00",
          "tree_id": "ab6599be1bda11b6a5414f0ed553f6caddc4e70f",
