          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a8b6f57ea7bb15e992e80dd4a6e3feeed4537fb3",
          "message": "Add color-mode toggle for watchers and chart\n\nIntroduce a ColorMode toggle (Auto/Range/Target/Worst) that drives the\nWatcherCard status rail and the PropertiesChart bars, coloring by a\nvalue's position within its acceptable range and/or its proximity to\nthe balancing target.\n\nThe `resolveStatusColor` resolver unifies the two, settling the\noverlapping-concerns question: Target has no fallback (gray when\nunset), Auto prefers the target when present else the range, and Worst\ntakes the more severe of the two.\n\nThe watcher range-meter marker stays tied to range position (that is\nwhat the meter depicts); only the slim status rail follows the toggle.\nThe controls are inline toolbar selects for now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-07T12:44:34-04:00",
          "tree_id": "85c0916039495ca7df54689a619a3a811ba1a5a4",
          "url": "https://github.com/ramonrsv/sci-cream/commit/a8b6f57ea7bb15e992e80dd4a6e3feeed4537fb3"
