          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7fdbefff380e0275b72fa3f192ca3622b4829c1e",
          "message": "Add balancing UI responsiveness benchmarks\n\nAdd e2e benchmarks for the watchers/balancing workflow, which had no\ncoverage: target validation latency, balance operation latency, and\nauto-balance re-balance. Each runs against two target sets -- the\ntypical Auto-filter heuristic and the worst-case set of every\nbalanceable key -- since validation and the solve both scale with\ntarget count.\n\nSetup runs once per test so only the UI interaction is timed. Validation\nbenches observe the per-card issue marker, produced solely by\nvalidate_recipe_targets, so they are gated on real validation output.\nBalance benches alternate the pinned batch total to force a guaranteed\nrecipe change each run while solving the full target set, and dispatch\nthe click directly to keep Playwright's actionability overhead out of\nthe timed region. Results flow to the existing e2e dashboard via the\nshared results array.\n\nAdd watcher/balancing locator and setup helpers to the e2e util, and\nTODO.md entries to explore a rapid-update solve-under-load bench and\ndecoupling the post-balance re-validation from the recipe paint.\n\nRename ui-responsivness.spec.ts to recipe-responsiveness.spec.ts (fixing\nthe spelling) so the responsiveness benches follow a consistent\n<domain>-responsiveness scheme now that balancing is split out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
