          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d79f6a514863dd0183d6b3b5db48c22ac9ff7f74",
          "message": "Add intensive->extensive balancing translation\n\nMake ABV and the FPD keys (FPD, ServingTemp, HardnessAt14C) directly\ntargetable balancing keys, translated to equivalent Alcohol, AbsPAC,\nand AbsNetPAC proxy targets before solving:\n\n- Add `translate_balancing_targets`, the shared front door of\n  `balance_compositions` and `validate_balancing_targets`.\n- Classify keys Intensive/Extensive via `BalanceKey::extent`; the\n  operational driver for translation is `BalanceKey::proxy`.\n- Error on targets resolving to one solver key (`ProxyTargetClash`,\n  e.g. the ambiguous ABV + Alcohol) and on out-of-domain intensive\n  values (`UntranslatableTarget`); temperature-valued FPD targets are\n  exempt from the negative-target check.\n- Add `get_pac_from_fpd_interpolation`, the exact table inverse of the\n  forward FPD interpolation, making target round-trips exact.\n- Re-admit ABV and the FPD keys to `get_all_balanceable_keys`, restore\n  ABV in the typical keys, and add `get_all_native_balancing_keys`\n  (the maximal translation-free set), used by `Recipe::deevaporate`.\n\n* Switch from `AbsNetPAC` to `ServingTemp` as typical balancing key.\n\nAdopt the widened key set across the JS surface and the app:\n\n- Expose `get_all_native_balancing_keys` through WASM and a\n  `getAllNativeBalancingKeys` TS wrapper.\n- Watchers: drop the unbalanceable-key handling (hidden/disabled\n  target inputs, fill-skips) now that every watched key is\n  balanceable, and retire its unit/visual coverage and snapshots.\n- Default the Custom selection to exactly the typical balancing keys\n  and drop HardnessAt14C from the always-active auto keys.\n- Point benches and the e2e worst-case target set at the native\n  (translation-free) keys, which cannot proxy-clash; update the TS\n  bridge bench to the fused `(key, value, priority?)` targets API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
