          "distinct": true,
          "id": "df17a587dd98a734f76a3a9a81429f8c0b9d2cec",
          "message": "Refactor EntitySearch into shell + atoms\n\nEntitySearch is now just the search shell: input, source tabs, list\nwith selection, and the panel container. The default detail panel\n(header, load/delete buttons, comments textarea) is gone; consumers\nown the panel content via `renderDetailPanel` and compose the new\ndetail-panel atoms.\n\nThe atoms (`DetailPanelHeader`, `LoadAction`, `DeleteAction`,\n`EditableComments`) live in `_components/detail-panel.tsx` and emit\nthe same DOM as the previous inline code, so no visual changes.\nEach is independently tested.\n\nIngredientSearch and RecipeSearch each compose their own panel from\nthe atoms; RecipeSearch drops its inline `VersionCommentsEditor` in\nfavour of the shared `EditableComments`.\n\nEntitySearch's prop surface shrinks from 18 to 10. The runtime\n`throw` that enforced \"one of renderDetailBody or renderDetailPanel\"\nis gone with the dual-mode logic.\n\nAdds `DETAIL_PANEL_ACTION_ICON_SIZE = 14` in sizes.ts and names a\n`RecipeDetailPanelProps` interface picked off `RecipeSearchProps`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
