          "distinct": true,
          "id": "bce0897081c1ce0b032e8b4be452ff39e6a1c714",
          "message": "Make DairyLabelSpec saturated/trans fat optional\n\nsaturated_fat and trans_fat default to STD_SATURATED_FAT_IN_MILK_FAT\nand STD_TRANS_FAT_IN_MILK_FAT applied to total_fat when omitted.\nNutrition labels often round these to 0 for small servings; the\ncomputed defaults track total fat more accurately.\n\nDrops the estimated values from dairy.json (USDA entries where the\nsurvey didn't report trans fat, plus Medallion/Theland powders) and\nupdates compare-test ceilings, snapshots, and per-spec COMP values\naccordingly. Adds source-link comments for Fairlife and Leanfit, and\nfixes the USDA Sweetened Condensed Milk water reference (27.2g).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
