          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e5e5b9f130f4c35bbabaefddb46a86b4b9b5e672",
          "message": "Simplify the nalgebra least squares impl using SVD\n\n* The previous implementation was solving the (A^t * A) * (A^t * Y) form\n  of the linear least squares solution. This is not required when using\n  SVD (Singular Value Decomposition), a resolution to the least-squares\n  can be found directly from the decomposed pseudoinverse matrix.\n* Improve assertion failure logging and epsilon granularity in tests.",
