          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e211dd6d16113ac1f22341cd12c12446ce435a7f",
          "message": "Reject negative balancing targets\n\nEvery balanceable CompKey is non-negative, so a target < 0 is\nunreachable and almost certainly a caller bug. Add an error-severity\nNegativeTarget BalancingIssue (sibling to NonFiniteTarget), detect it\nin validate_balancing_targets, and skip negative targets in the\nwarning checks so they aren't double-flagged.\n\nRemove the now-unnecessary .abs() on targets in row_weights and the\nbalance_rel_error_pp test helper, which previously silently floored\nnegative targets and hid such bugs.\n\nGuard the raw solver path (balance_with_reweighting) with a debug-only\nprecondition check that the targets carry no error-severity issue. The\nraw solvers assume pre-validated input; a bad target reaching them is a\nprogramming bug, not a user error, so it asserts in debug and compiles\nout in release.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-05T17:18:39-04:00",
          "tree_id": "fc7c77dbf113149a5ef0c3231982a5c4aa02af5a",
