          "distinct": true,
          "id": "acafd120e83324f1b31dc27f7b84f57fa08f84f9",
          "message": "Fix WASM use-after-free in search detail panels\n\nThe recipe and ingredient search detail panels freed their memoized\nMixProperties/Ingredient WASM object in a useEffect cleanup. Under\nReact Strict Mode (dev), the mount cycle runs setup -> cleanup ->\nsetup without recomputing the useMemo, so the cleanup freed the live\nobject that render still reads. The next re-render dereferenced a null\npointer, crashing with \"null pointer passed to rust\". This reproduced\nonly in `pnpm dev`, not in production.\n\nFree the previous instance once a new one supersedes it instead, never\nthe live one; the last instance is reclaimed by wasm-bindgen's\nFinalizationRegistry on unmount. Extract this into a shared\nuseFreeOnReplace hook and add StrictMode regression tests for both\npanels plus a focused unit test for the hook.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-11T01:45:01-04:00",
