          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ed4ea784b17f4592418d0f7f7f2b3269e109b6bd",
          "message": "Emit all balancing issues, dedup for display\n\nEach validation check now emits every issue it can detect; the\ncross-check ownership carve-outs in the palette pairwise, additive,\nand multi-ratio checks are gone. validate_balancing_targets then\ndeduplicates overlaps via a shared (whole, parts, direction) claim,\nkeeping the simplest framing (e.g. the palette-independent\nstructural issue over its dominance/ratio restatements).\n\nThe structural check now flags a strict subset of a roll-up's\ntargeted children that sums over the whole, a partial-rollup case\nthe old all-children/single-part checks missed.\n\nTests assert each raw generator's output and the deduplicated\nreport, so an absent issue is provably collapsed by dedup, not a\ngenerator that silently never fired.\n\nAlso rename are_equal_within_epsilon to are_equal, add the\nare_eq_flt_test test helper, and route the manual (x-y).abs() < eps\ncomparisons through the named helpers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-15T07:16:48-04:00",
          "tree_id": "fa30fd0cfd5a0c9377724b066668463995b31253",
