          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c39dcd7a849def840d747f1ed7712fe7ae2d33a3",
          "message": "Add web-vitals benchmark to track perf values\n\nNew track-only e2e benchmark that records actual Web Vitals values\nover time, complementing the existing pass/fail web-vitals test.\n\nCaptures the six standard web vitals plus Navigation Timing\nmilestones and an approximate hydration mark, averaged over 10 page\nloads, written to bench_output_web_vitals.json.\n\nThe App Router has no hydration-timing API, so WebVitals now sets an\n\"app-hydrated\" performance mark; its constant lives in a\ndependency-free module so the Playwright loader doesn't pull in\nnext/web-vitals.\n\nRuns as a separate bench:web-vitals script and a track-only\nweb_vitals_benchmarks CI job (fail-on-alert: false), since web\nvitals are noisier than the deterministic benches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-22T12:01:37-04:00",
