          "distinct": true,
          "id": "df7de7585599cd49887c6b2557ead896a3ed0de7",
          "message": "Simplify color helpers and hoist style constants\n\nReplace the per-color forwarders with getColor (theme-independent),\ngetJsColor(color, theme) (suffixes -light/-dark for canvas), and\ngetCssColor (var() for markup). Split the palette into a theme-\nindependent Color enum and a theme-dependent ThemeColor enum.\n\nHoist chart geometry and opacity magic numbers into named constants,\nand share RANGE_BAND_ALPHA, NO_RANGE_GRAY_ALPHA, and\nREFERENCE_TICK_ALPHA across the chart and watcher.\n\nStandardize two drifted values: the chart band tint (0.16 -> 0.25,\nmatching the meter band) and the watcher meter reference tick\n(0.6 -> 0.7, matching the chart tick). Both are intentional visual\ntweaks; snapshots to be regenerated.\n\nThese two tweaks fall below Playwright's default screenshot tolerance\n(threshold 0.2 YIQ): both are faint tints over light backgrounds, so\nthe per-pixel delta stays under the ~1409 cutoff and no pixels are\nflagged. The visual suite therefore passes without regeneration; the\ncommitted PNGs are stale-but-passing until refreshed.\n\nRemove dead code: REFERENCE_OPACITIES / getReferenceOpacity and the\nunused colorVarWithAlpha.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
