          "id": "d53dfd26f24de9591969d25db94bffd19da71d7c",
          "message": "Move FPD target translations into fpd curve API\n\nGive the fpd module a curve-point interface mirroring\n`compute_fpd_curves`, and rebuild the balancing translation layer's\nFPD math on top of it:\n\n- Add `compute_fpd_curve_point`, one `(frozen-water, hardness)` curve\n  point; `compute_fpd_curves` now delegates to it per point.\n- Add `compute_pac_from_fpd_curve_point`, its inverse: the PAC per\n  100 g of mix water putting a curve through `(frozen_water, fpd)`.\n  Both `PacToFpdMethod`s pair with their exact inverse conversion;\n  the summed-per-component `GoffHartel` curves method is rejected as\n  `UnsupportedFpdCurvesMethod` (no single-PAC inverse exists).\n- Add `DEFAULT_PAC_TO_FPD_METHOD` / `DEFAULT_FPD_CURVES_METHOD`\n  constants, shared by `FPD::compute_from_composition` and the\n  balancing translation — ready to become parameters later.\n- Translate the FPD balancing keys through the one inverse pinned at\n  each key's defining point: `FPD` at `(0, T)`, `ServingTemp` at\n  `(x_serve, T)`, `HardnessAt14C` at `(h, -14)`. The fpd module stays\n  in its PAC/water/hardness-factor vocabulary; the AbsPAC/AbsNetPAC\n  equivalence is documented in the translation layer.\n- Add `Error::FrozenWaterNotWithin100Percent` for the shared domain\n  check.\n- Test the inversions against forward-computed readings: exact\n  recovery from FPD and serving-temp readings, hardness recovery\n  within the measured `get_x_axis_at_fpd` linearization residual,\n  exact integer-hardness round-trips, and the domain/error cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
