          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7db105eeeec9312d1169511c5f3a41b6a0c433d0",
          "message": "Add make-recipe batch checklist and share link\n\nA batch is one weighing session covering one or more recipes, taken\nfrom the calculator slots or saved versions. Their rows merge into a\nsingle checklist with one column per recipe, so a shared ingredient\nis weighed off per recipe from one row.\n\nCheckoff state is keyed by a hash of the weighing content alone, so\nediting the title, date or notes keeps progress while changing an\namount resets it. That key falls out identically on both sides of a\nshare link, which carries the batch in the URL fragment and so never\nreaches the server.\n\nRecipes are told apart by a positional letter and hue. The letters\ncarry identity and the hues only reinforce it, since the palette is\nordered for colorblind separation rather than meaning.\n\nThe page doubles as the draft for the planned experiments record:\ndate and notes are on the batch so persisting one later is additive.\n\nLift the version chip out of the recipe editor so the batch builder\nlabels a version the same way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
