          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7f24fd429d55065da6e3132810fe32aad739253f",
          "message": "Extract EntitySearch shell from RecipeSearch\n\nLifts the search-bar + source-tab + two-column list/detail shell into a\ngeneric EntitySearch<E> in _components/entity-search.tsx, along with\nEntitySource (renamed from RecipeSource) and a free filterTaggedEntries\nhelper. Consumers supply embedded/saved entries, an id/displayName/match\ntrio, and render props for the list-item subtitle, header meta, and\ndetail body. Optional load (with slot picker), delete, and comments\nfeatures are wired through props.\n\nRefactors RecipeSearch to a thin wrapper around EntitySearch. Public\nexports preserved: RecipeSource is re-exported as an alias of\nEntitySource and TaggedEntry as Tagged<RecipeEntryJson>. The old\nfilterRecipeEntries function is dropped — it had no production callers\nand its source/query behaviour is covered by filterTaggedEntries; the\nrecipe-specific predicate is now exported as recipeMatchesQuery and\ntested directly. Recipe-specific labels (No recipes found., Delete\nsaved recipe, Recipe comments) flow through new EntitySearch props.\n\nAdds 32 tests for the generic shell covering filterTaggedEntries,\nlist/detail rendering, search and source filtering, delete and load\nwiring (including slot picker and confirm prompts), and the comments\neditor. The recipe-search test file collapses its 20-test\nfilterRecipeEntries block to 7 focused recipeMatchesQuery tests.\n\nPrepares for an IngredientSearch wrapper that reuses the same shell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-13T17:26:50-04:00",
          "tree_id": "2d5d5506b095adacc85f4a85450b45500fff2bd2",
