          "distinct": true,
          "id": "28db9ce664b8096c4373c38482d8395abd67634e",
          "message": "Add /ingredients search page\n\nWires up the previously-stub /ingredients route as an ingredient-library\nbrowser that mirrors the /recipes page in layout and behaviour, built on\nthe EntitySearch generic shell from the previous PR.\n\nAdds IngredientSearch in _components/ingredient-search.tsx, a thin\nwrapper around EntitySearch<SpecEntryJson> with embedded data from\nallSpecEntries (including alias entries). The detail panel shows the\nraw spec as pretty-printed JSON next to a CompositionView of the\nresolved Ingredient. When an entry has a comments field, its value is\nredacted to \"...\" in the JSON and the full text is rendered as a\nparagraph below the body via autoLink. Aliases display the resolved\ntarget's category plus an \"Alias\" badge in both the list subtitle and\nthe detail header. Search matches by name, by category for specs, and\nby target name for aliases.\n\nThe /ingredients page fetches the signed-in user's saved specs via the\nexisting fetchAllUserIngredientSpecs server action and coerces each\nrow's spec field into an IngredientSpecJson, accepting either a parsed\nobject or a JSON-encoded string and dropping malformed rows.\n\nRead-only on day 1: no save / edit / delete UI. Adds 37 unit tests for\nIngredientSearch (predicate, list, both detail-panel shapes, comments\nrendering and JSON redaction, read-only invariants, search filtering)\nand 7 for the page (adapter and signed-in/-out fetch wiring).\n\nAdds Playwright visual-regression coverage:\n__tests__/visual/ingredient-search.spec.ts (13 tests — empty state,\ningredient/alias/comments-bearing selection, search filtering, source\nfilters, active highlight, saved-entry detail) and an additional 9\nresponsive-layout snapshots for the page in __tests__/visual/layout.spec.ts.\nA selectIngredientByName helper parallels the existing\nselectRecipeByName, and recipe-search.spec.ts's \"detail panel scrolled\"\ntest now scrolls fully to the bottom.\n\nFixes two sources of nondeterminism that surfaced as flaky visual\ntests:\n- fetchAllUserIngredientSpecs and fetchAllUserSavedRecipes in\n  lib/data.ts now append ORDER BY name, giving production users and\n  tests a stable list. Two new ordering tests in lib/data.test.ts\n  cover both.\n- selectRecipeByName / selectIngredientByName anchor on the title\n  <span>'s exact text (via an inner .text-primary locator with an\n  escaped, anchored regex) instead of substring-matching the whole\n  button, so \"Sugar-Free Base\" no longer occasionally resolves to the\n  longer \"Sugar-Free Base (with user-defined)\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-14T10:41:54-04:00",
          "tree_id": "58a60d9b626ac4dc599e9e4061b7689eaaea2af4",
