          "distinct": true,
          "id": "ac40fbe3870e1afdee38df0daefea13f4576e9da",
          "message": "Estimate DairyLabelSpec MSNF from lactose + protein\n\nPreviously MSNF (or WS) was implicitly just lactose + protein, dropping\nthe ~10% mineral fraction that MSNF actually contains. Now the total is\nestimated from `(dairy_sugars + protein) / (1 - minerals_fraction)`,\nwith the fraction set per `SolidsSource` (Milk 10.5%, Whey 11.5%,\nCasein 10%), and capped at `(1 - 2%) * serving - fat - sucrose` to\nkeep powders within their typical max solids content.\n\nTightens accuracy vs. USDA reference water values significantly: e.g.\nSweetened Condensed Milk diff drops from 6.17% to 0.89%, Whole Milk\nfrom 0.70% to 0.37%, 2% Evaporated Milk from 1.85% to 0.91%. Powder\ncross-source correlation also improves sharply because the cap pins\nthe dry products near their real ~2% water content (Skim Milk Powder\nWater divergence 78.57% -> 23.29%).\n\nProtein-supplement labels under-report total composition, so the cap\nkicks in unevenly across sources and Water divergences grow there;\nthe model now exposes those label gaps rather than averaging them\naway (see updated narratives in compare_specs_whey_* and\ncompare_specs_casein_*).\n\nUpdates all DairyLabelSpec test fixtures and compare_specs ceilings\nand narratives to match the new values, and accepts the regenerated\ninsta snapshots. Tags ingredient JSON entries for whey/casein products\nwith `solids_source` so they pick the correct mineral fraction.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-26T17:48:38-04:00",
          "tree_id": "a478af97ba0f48e6e70d9da5a8b25ec2a79b4441",
