          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3eb55795832bfdca8795dfabdfe8e1356c8ee7f0",
          "message": "Support ratio keys as balancing targets\n\nEncode a ratio target R as the homogeneous row\n`numerator - (R/100)*denominator = 0`, so the solver never\ndivides and never NaNs on a zero denominator. Ratio keys\n(AbsPAC, StabilizersPerWater, EmulsifiersPerFat) are now\nfirst-class targets instead of being rejected.\n\nWeight each ratio row relatively via a denominator estimate\nD-hat (denominator-as-target, else 100-TotalSolids, else a\ntypical-mix constant), then correct it with one conditional\nreweight pass against the achieved denominator.\n\nMake is_unaffectable ratio-aware: a ratio whose numerator or\ndenominator no ingredient can affect is dropped and warned,\navoiding a degenerate NaN solve.\n\nRemove the now-obsolete RatioKeyTarget validation error and\nwiden get_balanceable_comp_keys to all keys. Note a TODO to\nreject negative targets explicitly.\n\nMove the balancing weight and estimate constants into a\nconstants::balancing module.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-04T15:10:15-04:00",
