          "distinct": true,
          "id": "44fccc3ad7a4b81db17fac39f2b4afa58b0e37ba",
          "message": "Return balancing report as a flat view for WASM\n\n`validate_recipe_targets` now returns each issue as a flat\n`{ severity, keys, message }` view instead of the structured\n`BalancingIssue` union. Severity, affected keys, and the\nhuman-readable message are all derived in Rust (new\n`BalancingIssue::affected_keys`, plus the existing `severity` and\n`Display`), so the TS side no longer hand-mirrors the issue\nvariants.\n\nDrops the nine per-variant types and `getBalancing{Errors,Warnings}`\nfrom `ts/balancing.ts` in favour of `BalancingIssueView`; a new\n`wasm::balancing` module holds the serializable view. Adding an\nissue variant is now Rust-only and compiler-enforced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-08T21:21:10-04:00",
          "tree_id": "453d4b3fe9aae42fd7a55de8f09b8e305e9394d2",
