          "id": "c63a25a8e89c2fa55f78b23499beb2d38909a496",
          "message": "Consolidate selects behind a shared Select\n\nExtract a single generic `Select`, a native `<select>`, and route\nRecipeSelect, QtyToggleSelect, KeyFilterSelect, the recipe-search\nversion picker and detail-panel's slot picker (LoadAction) through\nit, replacing the separate native `<select>` each previously owned.\nThe shared component maps arbitrary option values to and from option\nindices, so it works for non-string value types. ThemeSelect keeps\nits own Headless UI listbox trigger, which it already used, since a\nnative `<option>` can't render its per-option icons.\n\nRename the now-misnamed `.select-input` (its last user is a plain\ninput) to `.boxed-input`, and add a `.select-option` class for\nThemeSelect's menu rows.\n\nTests drive the widgets via implementation-agnostic helpers\n(selectOption, getSelectedOptionLabel, getSelectControl, and the\n*ByLabel variants) in unit/select.ts and e2e/select.ts, so a future\nswap of the underlying control only touches those helper bodies; the\ne2e helpers also handle ThemeSelect's listbox.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-10T22:32:51-04:00",
          "tree_id": "4f8a79ac1c1e8e906136a98fa3f3286c3710404c",
