          "distinct": true,
          "id": "68a7b442a7feed9b6cb430cc5f85e97175fc0b67",
          "message": "Expose CompKey hierarchy over WASM with a TS helper\n\nAdd `comp_hierarchy()`, which serializes the hierarchy forest in a\nsingle boundary crossing by deriving `Serialize` on `HierarchyNode`\n(no separate view type — the node already flattens to `{ key,\nchildren }`). The forest is faithful to the DAG: shared keys appear\nunder each parent, leaving projection to the caller.\n\nAdd `ts/hierarchy.ts`: `getCompHierarchy` returns the nested forest\nwith keys typed as `PropKey` (the serde variant-name string is\nalready a valid `PropKey`, so no conversion is needed and FPD/ratio\nkeys fold in later). `groupEnabledKeys` reorders an enabled key list\ninto hierarchy order with enabled-relative depth; its `duplicates`\noption chooses whether a shared key collapses to its first occurrence\nor repeats under each enabled roll-up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-11T18:43:34-04:00",
