          "distinct": true,
          "id": "9887e6ac961b43bedb9560294b3acb4a3e8120dd",
          "message": "Unify palette ratio checks into one subset search\n\nReplace the four overlapping palette enumerators (pairwise,\npairwise-ratio, additive, multi-ratio) with one depth-capped DFS\nover numerator subsets per single-key denominator. It feeds the\nshared band primitive and reports the minimal off-band subset,\nrendering the max <= 1 ordering corner as the friendlier\nDominanceViolation and anything else as a RatioInfeasibility.\nSingle/single pairs are reported from one orientation only.\n\nThis closes the >= 3-key gap the pairs-only checks missed: a\nnumerator group that overshoots the band though no pair does.\n\nThe unified search emits every overlap unconditionally and composes\nwith the existing emit-all flow: its issues pass through the\ngroup_claim deduplication, which collapses a part/whole overshoot\nagainst a StructuralViolation and an undershoot ratio against a\nRollupSumMismatch. This drops the structural-ownership skip, whose\ntransitive is_part_of test wrongly suppressed overshoots the\ndirect-only structural check never re-emits. The now-unused\ndominates helper is removed.\n\nAdapt the raw-generator tests to the single palette entry point,\nrelax the group assertions to the minimal subset, and add the\nthree-key overshoot and transitive-overshoot tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-16T23:37:43-04:00",
          "tree_id": "e34828d5294ed833d208c85e9a2327f8d12fcba5",
