          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7c9a7747317e22a0b19cfc0d811ae95f9c43e9cb",
          "message": "Debug assert only errors in balance_with_reweight*\n\n* `balance_with_reweighting` has a debug assert which checks that the\n  targets have been validated, since it explicitly skips validation for\n  performance reasons. This was calling `validate_balancing_targets`,\n  which does the full validation, including warning-severity issues. The\n  assert only triggers if there are errors, so we can do only the error\n  checks via `append_input_error_issues`, which greatly speeds up tests.\n* Use `HashSet` instead of `Vec` in `append_input_error_issues`. It\n  doesn't seem to impact performance, but is a better semantic fit.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-21T22:21:10-04:00",
