          "distinct": true,
          "id": "09a4833e8e14d8c71a0f679c89d6ab1fa4592f1b",
          "message": "Add egg source split and USDA egg ingredients\n\nAdd an EggSource {WholeEgg, EggWhite, EggYolk} field to EggSpec. The\nsource splits both solids and protein between white and yolk, and\nlecithin is now derived from the yolk-solids fraction rather than\nbeing a spec input (the lecithin field is removed).\n\nAdd the supporting egg composition constants (white/yolk mass, solids,\nprotein, and lecithin fractions) with USDA FoodData Central and\nliterature provenance.\n\nAdd 12 egg ingredients: Clarke and Goff & Hartel yolk (incl. dry), and\nUSDA raw/frozen/dried yolk, white, and whole egg. The consolidated\n\"Egg Yolk\" entry now links to its per-source variants.\n\nRecomputing Egg Yolk lecithin (9 -> 9.31) shifts the emulsifier-driven\nbalancing snapshots and doctests slightly. Also tidies the unrelated\n[^67] coffee-oil citation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
