          "distinct": true,
          "id": "494cabe8215f2d737b032d1989db9c6c352e5e64",
          "message": "Add ingredient locking to recipe balancing\n\nBalancing can now hold chosen ingredients fixed while the rest\nbalance around them, e.g. a flavouring whose amount is chosen for\ntaste rather than composition. A locked line still counts toward\nthe targets but keeps its amount.\n\nThe crate entry point balance_compositions folds each lock into its\ncomposition tuple, &[(Composition, Option<f64>)], so a lock cannot\nbe misaligned from its composition. Recipe::balance and the WASM\nbridge take &[(usize, Lock)], where Lock is Fraction (of the mix,\nconcentration-preserving) or Amount (grams, absolute), making the\ntotal-change semantics explicit instead of an implicit choice.\n\nThe nnls/nalgebra solvers and validate_balancing_targets share the\ntuple shape. Palette-derived feasibility warnings are skipped while\nany line is locked (a documented follow-up). Adds the Lock and\nBalanceLocks TypeScript types.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-08T00:06:58-04:00",
          "tree_id": "ca13bd68488bc529b623005e9ac0bdad82cee74f",
          "url": "https://github.com/ramonrsv/sci-cream/commit/494cabe8215f2d737b032d1989db9c6c352e5e64"
