          "distinct": true,
          "id": "14bcff5b7524261c8c4ce54de51c02191f9e6527",
          "message": "Support water evaporation in the calculator app\n\nThread the crate's `evaporation` recipe attribute through the Next.js\napp (phases 6-7 of the evaporation work).\n\n- lib/recipe.ts: add `evaporation` to RecipeSummary/RecipeStore/\n  RecipeUpdates, an `effectiveMixTotal` helper, localStorage round-trip,\n  and pass evaporation to the mix-properties bridge call.\n- Display denominators (properties table, composition-breakdown totals)\n  convert per-100g values to grams via the post-evaporation yield.\n- Recipe editor: Evap (g) toolbar input, inline yield in the Total row,\n  and a de-evaporate button; the recipe name moves to its own row.\n- Read-only RecipeTable / recipe-search: yield in the Total row and an\n  evaporation readout in the reserved toolbar band.\n- watchers: forward evaporation to validate/balance.\n- Load paths: carry evaporation through embedded recipe entries and the\n  localStorage load path (DB unchanged).\n\nWater-based input gating and sci-cream error handling are a follow-up.\n\n* Now that the ingredient name consumes an extra row, the table\n  overflows at the default panel height, so there is always a scrollbar\n  by default. Add a temporary hack to render one fewer row, in order to\n  avoid the scrollbar. This can be removed once height-adaptive\n  rendering is implemented for RecipeEditor and CompositionBreakdown.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
