          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1a74a9f59209febc145fd5e8ad4930b93fe02037",
          "message": "Fold per-target priority into balancing targets\n\nReplace the parallel `targets`/`priorities` lists with a single\n`targets: &[(BalanceKey, f64, Option<Priority>)]` across the crate,\nWASM boundary, TS types, and the app. This removes the\n`PriorityWithoutTarget` and `DuplicatePriority` issues: the former is\nnow structurally impossible, the latter subsumed by `DuplicateTarget`.\n\nThe JS boundary accepts 2- or 3-element target tuples via a\n`#[serde(default)]` deserialization shim, so unprioritized targets\nstay a compact `[key, value]` pair.\n\nNote: the `balancing_issues_report_input_errors` snapshot changes as a\nresult; its `.snap.new` is left for review and not included here, so\nthat test is red until the snapshot is accepted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-11T05:33:41-04:00",
