          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6498010a61fbcb502162d1ebc0f60ecb15801f1c",
          "message": "Add update-changelog skill for release prep\n\nAdd a skill that rewrites a package's `[Unreleased]` CHANGELOG section\nfrom the commits since its last release tag, and writes a companion\n`changes.log` report accounting for every commit as either cited by an\nentry or skipped with a reason. Takes `sci-cream`/`app`, defaults to\nboth, stops for review, and commits only on an explicit go-ahead.\n\nIt encodes the existing conventions: one line per entry with nested\ngroups as the only escape hatch, a 100-char limit that Prettier does\nnot check, keepachangelog section order, and end-state-only semantics.\n\nThe changelog commit it writes names the upcoming version, which the\nmanifest does not hold yet at that point, so the skill reads the\nmanifest and asks for the bump level rather than assuming one. The\nsubject form `for <ver> release` fits both packages, at 49 chars for\nthe crate and 43 for the app, where the older `for upcoming <ver> rel`\nform is 54 for the crate and does not fit.\n\nThree traps found while validating it against the current crate cycle:\n\n- `cargo release changes` under-reports. It resolves the package file\n  list at HEAD, so commits touching only paths since renamed drop out\n  silently: it lists 89 commits where `git log` lists 93, the four\n  missing ones touching only `src/balancing.rs`, which bd502308 split\n  into `src/balancing/`. The app's `release.sh` filters by directory\n  and has no such blind spot, so the skill treats `git log` as\n  authoritative and requires cross-checking it.\n- `cargo release changes` writes entirely to stderr, so a pipe without\n  `2>&1` yields nothing, with no error.\n- The `git log` cross-check needs a `:/`-anchored pathspec: the listing\n  step leaves the shell inside the package directory, where a bare path\n  matches nothing and prints zero commits.\n\nIgnore `/packages/*/changes.log`, since both release tools stage the\nwhole package directory and would otherwise sweep the report into the\nrelease commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
