          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2ff3bd1fca9a442e6048254913350ac8aabcf428",
          "message": "Add hover/tap drawer sidebar, hidden on mobile\n\nThe sidebar now hides on mobile (w-0) to reclaim horizontal space and\nbecomes an overlay drawer instead of pushing content:\n\n- Desktop: hovering the sidebar or header controls peeks the drawer\n  open; a dedicated toggle button pins it expanded or collapses it.\n- Mobile: a hamburger button opens the drawer (peek), the toggle pins\n  the collapsed rail, and a touch outside the sidebar/header dismisses.\n\nBoth sidebar and header-left render as absolute overlays over an\nin-flow spacer, with widths driven by the `sm:` breakpoint and a new\nuseIsDesktop hook branching the hover-vs-tap behavior. The spacer also\nreserves a small left gutter on mobile so content isn't flush against\nthe edge while the drawer is hidden.\n\nAdds unit tests for the sidebar collapse/peek states and the\nuseIsDesktop hook, and updates the visual/e2e navbar tests for the\nnew controls.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-23T23:34:53-04:00",
          "tree_id": "96dc6906fc59bd5a1ee453467e6c32cdfc63f7f1",
