          "distinct": true,
          "id": "67995eac478104041381539e778c74978c5d8201",
          "message": "Add relative-error weighting to balancing\n\nBalancing solved a plain (absolute) least-squares problem, so large\ntargets (Energy ~200) were fit closely while small ones (POD ~0.5,\nstabilizers) were effectively ignored. Weight each target row by\n1 / max(|target|, floor) so the solver minimizes relative error, and\ngive the mass-balance row a fixed dominant weight so the amounts still\nsum to 1 (an over-constrained boozy mix previously collapsed to 0.29).\n\nDrop targets no ingredient can affect (an all-zero column): such a row\nonly adds a constant to the objective but degrades the nnls solve.\n\nbalance_compositions_nalgebra/_nnls gain an Option<Weighting> argument\n(None = Relative); the Weighting enum is public for explicit absolute\nvs. relative comparison. Update tests, quality snapshots, and benches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-01T22:43:41-04:00",
