          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6b50314fe010ab25f88260923e3e87762f0e5e5c",
          "message": "Show watcher balancing issues in a toolbar chip\n\nValidation errors/warnings previously rendered in an inline strip\nbetween the toolbar and the card grid, which pushed every card down\nwhen issues appeared and shifted further when the strip expanded.\n\nMove the summary into a compact toolbar chip (per-severity counts)\nand render the detail list as a portal popover, so surfacing issues\nno longer displaces the grid. The popover dismisses on outside click\nor Escape and reuses the existing .popup style.\n\nDrive the red/amber severity colors from new err/warn theme tokens,\nconsumed by the .msg-* message boxes and by .issue-text-* /\n.issue-border-* accent classes for the chip counts and card marks.\n\nAlong the way: fix the Balance button's dead border-rd-lt (now the\nreal issue-border-error class), add the missing --color-graph-red\ntoken for the existing Color.GraphRed enum, rename KeyFilterSelect's\npopup state to popupPos, and drop the redundant typeof guard on\nvalidate_recipe_targets (the real Bridge always has it; try/catch\nstill covers runtime failures).\n\nAdd watchers.spec.ts visual-regression tests for the issues popover\nand the error/warning card highlights, with reference snapshots.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
