          "distinct": true,
          "id": "6a8dee1c58ce0d121ea52c0db187a3959e197ebd",
          "message": "Add CompKey part/whole hierarchy module\n\nEncode how CompKey roll-ups decompose into their parts as a single\nforest of explicit HierarchyNode literals. The relation is a DAG: a key\nmay sit under more than one parent (MilkFat under both TotalFats and\nMilkSolids), so shared keys simply repeat in the forest, macronutrient\ntrees first.\n\nA lazily-built index exposes the edges — children() (a roll-up's parts,\nwhich never exceed it in any composition) and parents() (the inverse,\nforest order) — plus the raw forest and a faithful pre-order\n(comp_hierarchy / comp_hierarchy_ordered / comp_hierarchy_roots). The\nmodule stays display-agnostic: projecting the DAG to a render tree (e.g.\nkeeping a shared key's first occurrence) is left to the caller.\n\nTests assert the subset invariant for every edge, exact equality for\nresidual-free roll-ups (parts pulled from the hierarchy), milk's nested\nsubset chain, branch uniqueness, and the pre-order shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
