          "distinct": true,
          "id": "b9ad14449d16ed48645baf246990b82b59e6bc9e",
          "message": "Unify balancing checks on ratio-band primitive\n\nConsolidate the feasibility checks in validate_balancing_targets onto a\nsingle ratio_band primitive: the convex-hull-achievable band of a group\nratio Σnum/Σden (empty denominator = absolute magnitude). Every check is\nnow a thin enumerator that picks (numerator, denominator) groups and\nfeeds the shared comparator rather than hand-rolling band math.\n\n- Merge pairwise + additive dominance into one grouped\n  DominanceViolation, and add a grouped RatioInfeasibility for off-band\n  ratios (e.g. a pinned CocoaButter:CocoaSolids ratio). The additive\n  subset-sum group now feeds the full band: its upper corner stays a\n  DominanceViolation, its lower corner becomes a RatioInfeasibility,\n  catching a palette-pinned share (e.g. the named sugars summing to all\n  of TotalSugars yet targeted below it).\n- Add palette-independent structural checks driven by the hierarchy\n  forest: StructuralDominanceViolation (a part target above its whole)\n  and RollupSumMismatch (residual-free rollup completeness). They run\n  first and own only the ordering corner, so palette enumerators keep\n  their skips narrow: a part/whole pair still gets the ratio-band\n  check; only its dominance issue is suppressed.\n- Give RatioKey targets a reachability check (previously skipped).\n- Add a Severity::Info advisory tier with OverDetermined; thread the\n  \"information\" string through the WASM view and TS IssueSeverity.\n\nAdd CompKey::is_part_of and is_residual_free_rollup hierarchy helpers,\na round2 display formatter, and render the new tier in watcher-issues.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-14T04:37:57-04:00",
