          "distinct": true,
          "id": "07f73df453c4369840d3bf3f293eb23bca2413ef",
          "message": "Convert dairy mL servings via modeled density\n\nDairyLabelSpec now converts an mL serving size to grams by solving a\nfixed point on the dairy density, which depends on the fat, MSNF, and\nsucrose fractions that themselves depend on the serving size. The\ndensity model is selected by composition: the fat-only fresh fit for\nfresh milk/cream, and the (fat, MSNF, sucrose) linear fit for\nconcentrated or sweetened dairy.\n\nThis also fixes a bug where a grams-labeled fat was passed to the\nconversion as if it were a fat percentage.\n\nThe Carnation evaporated and Eagle Brand sweetened-condensed entries\nnow specify their mL serving directly instead of a hand-converted gram\nweight, letting the model derive the density.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-20T03:29:40-04:00",
          "tree_id": "cc2e2ed9d998587db679da336bc1ca0884003b22",
          "url": "https://github.com/ramonrsv/sci-cream/commit/07f73df453c4369840d3bf3f293eb23bca2413ef"
