          "distinct": true,
          "id": "84e3ca7218b3ea458bf25ba7bfc67a413436a058",
          "message": "Add warmup and robust stats to e2e benchmarks\n\nanalyzeMeasurements now returns an outlier-robust central value (a\n10% trimmed mean for n>=10, else the median) and the trimmed-sample\nstandard deviation as the spread, replacing the raw mean/stdDev.\nBenchmarkResult's avg/stdDev fields are renamed central/spread.\n\nThe shared time/memory e2e helpers gain a warmupRuns param (default\n1) that discards leading cold runs before recording, so a cold\nJIT/cache/server first run no longer drags the average. Timing and\nweb-vitals keep one warmup.\n\nMemory opts out (warmupRuns 0): the median of its runs already\nabsorbs a cold/spiky run, and a memory run is too expensive to spend\none on. Its recorded runs go 2 -> 3 for a meaningful median and the\ntimeout 5 -> 8 min.\n\nAdds a unit test for analyzeMeasurements.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
