          "id": "41844fa3ab12c90170edead5e5eb8ddc002e4d80",
          "message": "De-flake recipe-resources e2e timing tests\n\nThe user-defined \"resilient to slow fetches\" test measured time from\npage.goto(), so navigation and hydration jitter under worker\ncontention pushed it past its thresholds. Anchor timing instead to\nthe stalled server-action POST's issuance via waitForRequest, so the\nwindow covers only the stall and the interaction.\n\nFor the no-user-defined test, add a deterministic assertion that the\npath issues zero user-data server-action POSTs, alongside the\nexisting wall-clock check. This catches a regression that makes the\npath POST-dependent regardless of how its stall overlaps page load.\n\nExtract an isUserDataServerAction predicate and reuse it for the\nslow-fetch stall route, both request counters, and the new wait.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
