          "id": "dc2020e9f87061fc183958e9ff9ef9c709d2b399",
          "message": "Fix Watchers/Properties toolbar overflow wrapping\n\nThe shared .toolbar stacked its flex row-gap on top of the items'\nown vertical margins, so wrapped rows looked over-spaced. Switch to\ngap-y-0 so inter-row spacing comes from the item margins alone.\n\nThe Watchers right-side controls were one non-wrapping shrink-0 block\nthat overflowed off-screen (clipping the Balance button) at narrow\nwidths. Regroup them into four clusters (issues, fill buttons, total,\nauto+balance) in a right-aligned flex-wrap container so they wrap\ntogether onto the next row instead of being cut off.\n\nRegenerate the affected toolbar and calculator visual snapshots.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
