          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a4e1595cec234949b35ff28dd2107fc079209e54",
          "message": "Extract URL payload codec and copyable field\n\nRecipe share shipped with its codec monomorphic over SharePayload\nand its reusable primitives module-private, so a second payload\nkind could not reuse them without duplicating security-critical\nparsing.\n\n- New `url-payload.ts` owns the transport: JSON -> deflate-raw ->\n  base64url, the size caps, and `comparePayloadVersion`. It is\n  generic over a caller-supplied validator, with caps as options\n  and an injected error factory, so each payload kind keeps its\n  own branded error type and user-facing copy.\n- `transformBytes` now throws a private `SizeLimitExceeded`\n  sentinel, translated at the `decodeUrlPayload` boundary. Generic\n  code cannot `instanceof` the caller's error, and without the\n  sentinel a decoded-size overrun would surface as Invalid rather\n  than TooLarge.\n- `validate` is called outside the try, so branded validator errors\n  propagate unwrapped instead of being rewrapped as Invalid.\n- `recipe-share.ts` now delegates to it, keeping its exported API\n  and every `SHARE_ERROR_MESSAGES` string unchanged.\n- Lift `CopyButton` and `CopyableField` out of the share dialog\n  into `copyable-field.tsx`; both are generic, and other dialogs\n  need them.\n\n`recipe-share.test.ts` is unmodified and still passes, which is the\ncheck that the refactor preserved behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
