          "id": "f7aa5032c90583c39d1f31a28dcc3ae0eddab605",
          "message": "Add filename-redundancy convention; align lib dirs\n\nCodify when a filename may repeat its directory's category word:\ndrop it by default (the dir + exported symbol carry the role), keep\nit only for base/eponymous modules, control/wrapper kinds\n(selects/*-select, *-provider, use- hooks), or too-generic tokens.\nThis ratifies selects/-select vs tables/-drop as principled.\n\nApply the rule to the lib feature dirs, keeping base batch.ts and\nrecipe.ts:\n\n- resources/  session-resources -> session, wasm-resources -> wasm\n- batch/      batch-builder -> builder, batch-colors -> colors,\n              batch-share -> share\n- recipe/     recipe-share -> share\n\nOnly the @/lib/... prefixes and co-located test imports change.\nDocument the convention in CLAUDE.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
