          "distinct": true,
          "id": "29f9f141ca675faaf01c3348ed6041f48a47da25",
          "message": "Enable grid resize, scroll, and sticky tables\n\nCollapse the table styling onto one presentational `.table-col-header`\n(borders + a zero-layout inset-shadow top edge) and make stickiness\nopt-in: a table freezes its header by sticking its own `<thead>` via\n`.table-sticky-head`, and pins columns with `.table-pin-head` (head\nband, z-20) / `.table-pin-cell` (body band, z-10) paired with a\n`left-{offset}` utility. This removes the `.table-static`/`.table-flow`\nmarkers entirely.\n\n- Composition breakdown is one scrollable table with pinned Ingredient\n  and Qty columns; the header and totals freeze together.\n- RecipeTable (recipes/ingredients detail panels) header now flows with\n  the shared scroll pane instead of detaching on scroll.\n- Make every calculator panel resizable on both axes and drop the fixed\n  panel heights; bump LAYOUT_VERSION to reset stored layouts.\n- Teach the visual-test stitcher to de-duplicate a sticky `<thead>`:\n  crop it after the first frame and shrink the scroll step by its\n  height, so it appears once and no occluded content is lost.\n- Select breakdown comp columns via `data-comp-key` in tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
