          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d1aa86e093efe838d4bbe651a3142fd4c9cd61c5",
          "message": "Display balancing targets in PropertiesBarChart\n\nLift the watcher targets map out of WatchersView into the calculator\npage as persisted state, threaded like the auto-balance state (plain\nprop tuples, no React context): read/write into WatchersPanel and\nread-only into PropertiesChartPanel.\n\nWatchersView keeps a local persisted fallback when no caller-owned\ntargetsState is provided, so standalone renders stay self-contained;\nthe fallback only touches storage when it is the owner.\n\nThe chart draws targets as one more tick-marker series through the\nrange-meter plugin (RefMarker generalized to TickMarker): solid blue\nto match WatcherCard's target tick, drawn over the reference ticks,\nwith legend and tooltip entries. Zero targets are kept (deliberate),\nunset/NaN dropped; target values join the value-axis max so ticks\naren't clipped.\n\nAdd visual regression coverage for the chart's target ticks (Main\nalone, Main plus both references, and horizontal orientation) via a\nnew presetWatcherTargets e2e helper.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-05T15:45:17-04:00",
          "tree_id": "fd81075afb6baaff9f1741546ef8806b16cb0dba",
