          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5496fb7612102b76de05744099632cc8d06768d1",
          "message": "Support locking ingredient rows at zero amount\n\nA locked zero-amount row is now held at 0 g, pinning the ingredient\nout of the balance (kept at zero) while the rest solve around it.\nOnly an unset (empty) quantity cannot be locked.\n\n- recipe.ts: extract a shared isLockable predicate (a set quantity,\n  including zero) as the single source of truth for the editor lock\n  control and makeBalanceLocks, which now emits { Amount: 0 } for a\n  locked zero row. Trim the isLockable/makeBalanceLocks docs.\n- recipe.tsx: use the shared predicate, so the lock control shows on\n  zero-amount rows.\n- recipe.rs: test that a zero-amount lock holds the line at 0 g while\n  the rest rebalance (the crate already supported it).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-08T17:41:18-04:00",
          "tree_id": "03588af944c94a7ea4dd09cb8f22cb363ec18fe4",
