          "id": "092e02515a98629d1a4ae1465f8edff68eca6a82",
          "message": "Add auto-balance rapid-update settle benchmark\n\nMeasure how long the UI takes to absorb a burst of rapid target\nupdates with auto-balance on, per target set (auto, all targets).\nEach timed run fires 50 distinct pinned totals back-to-back with no\nawait between fills, letting intermediate solves coalesce, then awaits\nthe final total's settled recipe. Reported as total burst-to-settle\ntime (not per-update), so coalescing reads as the win it is.\n\nThis complements the single-shot re-balance bench: that isolates\nper-solve latency, this isolates burst throughput under load.\n\nSettled reset/final signatures are captured once so each run awaits\nthem by positive equality, avoiding a transient mid-solve match. Drop\nthe now-implemented rapid-update entry from TODO.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
