          "distinct": true,
          "id": "efa6e23c2a8353bd04a47b78bb4ab0a950861846",
          "message": "Add recipe share links (/share and /share/embed)\n\nStateless sharing: the whole recipe is encoded in the URL fragment\n(JSON -> deflate-raw -> base64url), never sent to the server. The\nversioned payload carries name, rows, optional evaporation and\ncomments, and optionally inlined user-defined ingredient specs.\n\n- /share viewer: read-only recipe detail (table, mix properties,\n  comments) on an ephemeral WASM bridge (never seeds the session\n  bridge); \"Open in calculator\" writes a localStorage slot. Like\n  the editor, mix properties are calculated from the rows that\n  resolve (unresolved rows are flagged red with a warning), and a\n  throwing calculation degrades to empty properties via mixError.\n- Shared RecipeDetailBody element renders the detail body (toolbar\n  spacer + evaporation readout, fixed-height properties view,\n  comments below) for both the recipe-search detail panel and the\n  share viewer; a mixError flags the evaporation readout red.\n- /share/embed: chromeless iframe-friendly variant with a \"View\n  full recipe\" link; frame-ancestors 'self' globally with * on the\n  embed route only.\n- Share dialog in the recipe editor toolbar and recipe-search\n  detail panel: copyable link and iframe snippet, opt-in\n  per-ingredient consent before inlining user-defined specs, and\n  an opt-out \"Include comments\" checkbox.\n- Strict payload validation: compressed/decoded size caps enforced\n  during streaming inflation, shape checks, row/name/comment/spec\n  limits, and friendly error states with no partial loads.\n- Harden localStorage access: sandboxed third-party iframes throw\n  SecurityError on any window.localStorage touch; treat as absent.\n- Tests: unit (payload round-trip, caps, malformed, versioning;\n  viewer states, errors, and WASM lifetime; dialog consent and\n  comments checkboxes), e2e (share flows, consent, embed framing,\n  clickjacking block), and visual specs (snapshots to be generated\n  separately).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
