          "id": "2287c26573492ee9a7351a00f6d4c974e262cc49",
          "message": "Repaint charts on theme change via class observer\n\nThe charts read cascaded CSS colors during render, so they must\nre-render after the theme flips. The `next-themes` `resolvedTheme`\nsubscription fires too early: the `.dark` class is applied in a\npost-commit effect, so the re-render reads stale colors and the\ncanvas keeps the old palette until something else re-renders it.\n\nReplace the subscription with a `useThemeRepaint` hook that observes\nthe root class mutation and re-renders after it lands. Add a\nregression test to each chart asserting a class flip re-reads colors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-09T22:22:44-04:00",
          "tree_id": "95fe3dbdf85550b047b67ca2f0c2b7b8aebbe8c9",
