          "distinct": true,
          "id": "7868f9bc20460fe307ebebd198f5c4372a660e7d",
          "message": "Decouple target validation from proxy translation\n\nSplit the balancing translation front door into two independent\noperations, composed by the entry points:\n\n- `translate_balancing_targets` is now pure proxy substitution: fused\n  targets in, fused targets out, no issue reporting. Its precondition\n  (error checks run, flagged targets excluded) is documented, and an\n  out-of-domain proxy value panics as a caller ordering bug.\n  `TranslatedTargets` is gone.\n- The error-side checks live in the validate module, each following\n  the `append_*_error_issues` convention: the new\n  `append_untranslatable_error_issues` and\n  `append_proxy_clash_error_issues` join `append_input_error_issues`,\n  grouped in their fixed order by `append_target_error_issues`.\n- New `dropped_target_keys` derives which targets downstream\n  processing must drop from the reported issues (value-flagged keys\n  and clash-group members).\n- `balance_compositions` gates on the target and lock error checks\n  first, then translates — past the gate, translation never sees a\n  flagged target. `validate_balancing_targets` appends the target\n  errors, excludes the dropped keys, then translates for the warning\n  checks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-16T11:46:36-04:00",
