          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a2c1f5280459586b4f993d7ab24758402e81e30f",
          "message": "Unify invalid target values as OutOfDomainTarget\n\nEvery balancing key has an admissible target interval, and the old\n`NegativeTarget` / `UntranslatableTarget` split reported its two ways\nof being violated as unrelated issues, named after implementation\nmechanisms rather than the shared concept:\n\n- Add `BalanceKey::target_domain` — `[0, inf)` for quantity and ratio\n  keys, `(-inf, 0]` for the temperature keys, `[0, 100]` for hardness\n  — replacing `negative_target_allowed` and the untranslatable check\n  as the single home for per-key domain knowledge.\n- Replace both issue variants with `OutOfDomainTarget { key, value,\n  min, max }`, carrying the violated bounds like `UnreachableTarget`,\n  with one bounds-aware message (\"must be at least 0\" / \"at most 0\" /\n  \"between 0 and 100\") replacing the two mechanism-flavored ones.\n- Check it in `append_out_of_domain_error_issues`, one range test per\n  target; the input checks keep non-finite values and duplicates.\n- Point the raw-path debug assert at the whole target gauntlet, so it\n  again catches out-of-domain values after the negative check moved\n  out of the input checks.\n- Add a TODO follow-up: tighten the upper bound to 100 for `ABV` and\n  the mass-fraction `CompKey`s, exempting `Energy`, `POD`, and the\n  PAC family (sucrose equivalents untied to physical mass).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
