          "id": "4bbf56c1a3fe522645c0e33a7c833f6a4549e1d6",
          "message": "Add inline version-name controls to recipe editor\n\nReplace the version badge's static integer with the display name from\nthe saved-recipes cache, and add inline version controls to the name\nrow: a badge for the loaded version, a `→ new-version` input, and a\nbranch button that saves under the typed name (or the next name when\nblank). The branch button is always shown — disabled off the main\nrecipe or before the recipe's first save — while the `→` input appears\nonly on the main recipe, since reference slots can't be branched. The\noverwrite Save button moves flush to the right of the row.\n\nThe new-version input is grammar- and uniqueness-validated inline, and\nVersionBadge now accepts a string so named versions render as-is.\nDefault users who never opt in still see plain integers and one-click\nsave-as-new-version, unchanged.\n\nKeep the input's height from growing the name row (and shifting the\ntable on version load) with a `my-0!` override of boxed-input's\nunlayered `my-1`; note the underlying no-op-override issue in TODO.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-22T01:35:01-04:00",
